item.text:
{
  "concepts": [
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "F16, Engagement baseline, is an operational profile. Its foundation-to-law trace distinguishes imported consequences, foundational commitments, profile choices and adopting-Product choices. Inclusion in a method cut makes it available; adoption is a separate Product-authority act.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":198,
          "quote":"This member is material family F16, Engagement baseline (operational\nprofile).",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F3.%20Engagement%20applicability%2FFoundation%20to%20law",
          "start_line":197
        }
      ],
      "key":"engagement_baseline",
      "label":"Engagement baseline"
    },
    {
      "conditions":[],
      "definition":"An engagement frame evaluates selection, construction, assessment or disposition of governed work. Executive, Worker and Reviewer are the profile's engagement frames.",
      "exceptions":[],
      "grounding":[
        {
          "end_line":342,
          "quote":"An engagement frame is a frame (REFERENCE_FRAME §1) whose evaluation family\nconcerns selecting, constructing, assessing or disposing governed work.\nExecutive, Worker and Reviewer are this profile's engagement frames (P1;\nrc.2 #engagement-frame).",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F5.%20Profile%20terms%2FEngagement%20frame",
          "start_line":339
        }
      ],
      "key":"engagement_frame",
      "label":"Engagement frame"
    },
    {
      "conditions":[],
      "definition":"An activated Product, requirement, design, identity, release, domain, implementation, test, operational, historical or capability frame needed by one engagement evaluation.",
      "exceptions":[],
      "grounding":[
        {
          "end_line":348,
          "quote":"A specialist frame is an activated Product, requirement, design, identity,\nrelease, domain, implementation, test, operational, historical or\ncapability frame that one engagement evaluation needs.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F5.%20Profile%20terms%2FSpecialist%20frame",
          "start_line":346
        }
      ],
      "key":"specialist_frame",
      "label":"Specialist frame"
    },
    {
      "conditions":[],
      "definition":"A reusable evaluation-family archetype naming a recurring distinction. It selects no concrete carrier, component, actor, architecture, owner or implementation.",
      "exceptions":[],
      "grounding":[
        {
          "end_line":360,
          "quote":"A generic specialist-frame family is a reusable evaluation-family archetype\nof this profile (§11). It names a recurring distinction that a project\neither instantiates where material, has capable authority establish as\nnon-material for the governed outcome, or keeps as an explicit coverage\nresidual (P2, P6; rc.2 #generic-specialist-frame-family).",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F5.%20Profile%20terms%2FGeneric%20specialist-frame%20family",
          "start_line":356
        }
      ],
      "key":"generic_specialist_family",
      "label":"Generic specialist-frame family"
    },
    {
      "conditions":[],
      "definition":"Testing frame, authoritative Product path and material combinatorial complexity are tier-2 terms owned by ASSURANCE §7 and used here without additions.",
      "exceptions":[],
      "grounding":[
        {
          "end_line":373,
          "quote":"Testing frame, authoritative Product path and material combinatorial\ncomplexity are tier-2 terms defined in ASSURANCE §7. This profile uses them\nas defined there and adds nothing to them (P1; rc.2 #testing-frame,\n#authoritative-product-path, #material-combinatorial-complexity).",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F5.%20Profile%20terms%2FTerms%20owned%20by%20ASSURANCE",
          "start_line":370
        }
      ],
      "key":"assurance_owned_terms",
      "label":"ASSURANCE-owned terms"
    },
    {
      "conditions":[],
      "definition":"The frame selecting or confirming bounded activation configuration and consuming closed Worker and Reviewer results under existing project decision authority. Its complete Product view and current MVP or release mandate support priority, disposition and selection of the next authorised action; this view is not the complete workspace.",
      "exceptions":[],
      "grounding":[
        {
          "end_line":382,
          "quote":"Executive is this profile's label for the frame that selects or confirms\nthe bounded activation configuration and consumes closed Worker and\nReviewer results under existing project decision authority. It holds the\ncomplete Product view and the current MVP or release mandate needed to\nassign priority, apply disposition and select the next authorised action\n(P6, P2; rc.2 #executive).",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F5.%20Profile%20terms%2FExecutive",
          "start_line":377
        }
      ],
      "key":"executive",
      "label":"Executive"
    },
    {
      "conditions":[],
      "definition":"The ACTIVATION constructor role activated as a frame, owning construction and self-review within exact intake through operation authority inherited from the governing work relation. Writer is its document-and-record specialisation.",
      "exceptions":[],
      "grounding":[
        {
          "end_line":396,
          "quote":"Worker is this profile's label for the constructor role of ACTIVATION §1\nactivated as a frame. It owns construction and self-review inside its exact\nintake, through the operation authority inherited from the governing work\nrelation. It acquires no admission, publication, acceptance or continuation\nauthority (P6; rc.2 #worker).",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F5.%20Profile%20terms%2FWorker",
          "start_line":392
        }
      ],
      "key":"worker",
      "label":"Worker"
    },
    {
      "conditions":[],
      "definition":"An activated independent live-surface evaluation consumed by the assessment relation. It evaluates one exact subject and returns a closed result, adding evidence-bound technical triage when a finding exists.",
      "exceptions":[],
      "grounding":[
        {
          "end_line":407,
          "quote":"Reviewer is this profile's label for the independent live-surface\nevaluation that the assessment relation of ACTIVATION §1 consumes, governed\nby EVALUATION §3 (independence and traceability) and EVALUATION §1 and §7\n(assurance boundary and qualification freeze), activated as a frame. It\nevaluates one exact subject and returns a closed result, with evidence-bound\ntechnical triage when a finding exists.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F5.%20Profile%20terms%2FReviewer",
          "start_line":400
        }
      ],
      "key":"reviewer",
      "label":"Reviewer"
    },
    {
      "conditions":[],
      "definition":"Reviewer assessment of one finding against its exact evaluated claim and basis. Its supportable payload comprises affected claim and observed failure, Product-scaled severity, causal assessment and quantified-assurance confidence, blast radius and affected users/paths/relations, workaround or containment, repair complexity, regression risk, material dependencies, residual uncertainty and evidence that would reduce it.",
      "exceptions":[],
      "grounding":[
        {
          "end_line":423,
          "quote":"- the affected claim and the observed failure;\n- severity on the Product-selected severity scale;\n- causal assessment and confidence, the confidence being a quantified\n  claim under [FOUNDATIONS §4 Quantified assurance](FOUNDATIONS.md#quantified-assurance);\n- blast radius and the affected users, paths or relations;\n- an available workaround or containment;\n- repair complexity, regression risk and material dependencies; and\n- residual uncertainty and the evidence that would reduce it.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F5.%20Profile%20terms%2FTechnical%20triage%2C%20severity%2C%20priority%20and%20boundary%20effect",
          "start_line":416
        }
      ],
      "key":"technical_triage",
      "label":"Technical triage"
    },
    {
      "conditions":[],
      "definition":"Four distinct values are severity, priority, frame result and current-boundary effect. Severity grades a finding's consequence if manifested and is Reviewer evidence. Priority is an Executive decision ordering response relative to complete Product outcome, likelihood/exposure, MVP or release mandate, reversibility, dependencies, delay cost and capacity. Current-boundary effect records blocks, requires narrowing, or may remain an explicit residual; it is a decision projection with no independent core value or disposition.",
      "exceptions":[],
      "grounding":[
        {
          "end_line":434,
          "quote":"Severity grades the consequence if the finding manifests. Priority orders\nthe response relative to the complete Product outcome, likelihood and\nexposure, the current MVP or release mandate, reversibility, dependencies,\ncost of delay and available capacity. The Reviewer grades severity; the\nExecutive assigns priority (P6, P2).",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F5.%20Profile%20terms%2FTechnical%20triage%2C%20severity%2C%20priority%20and%20boundary%20effect",
          "start_line":430
        },
        {
          "end_line":456,
          "quote":"Current-boundary effect is the Executive's recorded determination of what\none finding does to the current promotion boundary: it blocks it, requires\nnarrowing it, or may remain an explicit residual. It is a decision\nprojection, a state this profile declares, not a result and not a\ndisposition (§8): it maps to no core value of its own and decides nothing\nby itself.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F5.%20Profile%20terms%2FTechnical%20triage%2C%20severity%2C%20priority%20and%20boundary%20effect",
          "start_line":451
        }
      ],
      "key":"finding_decision_values",
      "label":"Severity, priority, frame result and current-boundary effect"
    },
    {
      "conditions":["A Worker has been lawfully and successfully activated."],
      "definition":"The Worker's closed output to its declared consumer, which is the Executive in the coordinated branch. Construction availability has five total, exclusive values mapped to one core value each: candidate_ready→satisfied; refused→falsified; incomplete→falsified; re_entry_requested(authority)→out_of_frame; re_entry_requested(basis)→invalid_basis. These are carriers, neither assessment nor acceptance nor new dispositions.",
      "exceptions":[],
      "grounding":[
        {
          "end_line":490,
          "quote":"The work-result values are the five values of construction availability,\nthe refinement that\n[ACTIVATION §3](ACTIVATION.md#construction-availability) defines for the\npredicate \"a candidate is available\". ACTIVATION §3 owns their grounds,\nmaps each to exactly one core value, and states that the mapping is total\nand exclusive after lawful activation. In this profile they are carriers,\nnot new semantic dispositions, and none of them is an assessment or an\nacceptance of the candidate (FOUNDATIONS §4 Results).",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F5.%20Profile%20terms%2FWork%20result",
          "start_line":483
        }
      ],
      "key":"work_result",
      "label":"Work result"
    },
    {
      "conditions":[],
      "definition":"Subject identity required by transition evidence and traceability. It is frozen before material reference exposure where generic method qualification requires; elsewhere immutable identity or an equivalent exact-subject relation stabilises it sufficiently for the claimed assessment. This introduces no lifecycle state named frozen.",
      "exceptions":[],
      "grounding":[
        {
          "end_line":536,
          "quote":"An exact candidate is the subject identity that the transition evidence of\nACTIVATION §7 and the traceability of EVALUATION §3 require. Where generic\nmethod qualification applies (EVALUATION §7), its construction result is\nfrozen before material reference exposure as that clause requires.\nElsewhere this profile stabilises the review subject through an immutable\nidentity or an equivalent exact-subject relation sufficient for the claimed\nassessment. The profile creates no new lifecycle state named `frozen` (P3,\nP6; rc.2 #exact-candidate).",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F5.%20Profile%20terms%2FExact%20candidate",
          "start_line":529
        }
      ],
      "key":"exact_candidate",
      "label":"Exact candidate"
    },
    {
      "conditions":["The Product-owned Project Reference-Frame Basis adopts the profile."],
      "definition":"Projection inside the Product-owned basis recording selected profile mapping, exact outcome, actor envelopes, evidence coordinates and revision conditions additional to Product binding. It consumes that basis, creates no second basis and mints no projected authority.",
      "exceptions":[],
      "grounding":[
        {
          "end_line":546,
          "quote":"A baseline-adoption projection consumes the Product-owned Project\nReference-Frame Basis of PRODUCT_DEFINITION §7. Where that basis adopts\nthis profile, the projection records the selected profile mapping, exact\noutcome, actor envelopes, evidence coordinates and revision conditions\nneeded in addition to the Product binding (§16). It is not a second\nframe-basis definition and mints none of the authority it projects (P6;\nrc.2 #baseline-adoption-projection).",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F5.%20Profile%20terms%2FBaseline-adoption%20projection",
          "start_line":540
        }
      ],
      "key":"baseline_adoption_projection",
      "label":"Baseline-adoption projection"
    },
    {
      "conditions":[],
      "definition":"The Product-owned Project Reference-Frame Basis projects existing owners' decisions and cites every material configuration source without becoming a new local-axiom authority.",
      "exceptions":[],
      "grounding":[
        {
          "end_line":1443,
          "quote":"The Product-owned Project Reference-Frame Basis (PRODUCT_DEFINITION §7)\ncites every material source of the configuration and does not collapse\nthem into a new local-axiom authority (P6).",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F16.%20Adoption%20or%20project-defined%20configuration%2FExisting%20authority%20selects%20the%20configuration",
          "start_line":1441
        }
      ],
      "key":"project_reference_frame_basis",
      "label":"Product-owned Project Reference-Frame Basis"
    },
    {
      "conditions":[],
      "definition":"A finite decision-driven cycle maintaining the unresolved material-evaluation frontier and closed-result ledger, activating dependency-ready evaluations on exact outcome and basis and updating coverage, dependencies, conflicts and discovered materiality.",
      "exceptions":[],
      "grounding":[
        {
          "end_line":606,
          "quote":"U0 = every known material evaluation not closed on the current basis\n\nwhile U is non-empty:\n  select a finite dependency-ready subset M that fits the assigned actors\n  activate each member of M against the exact outcome and basis\n  keep assurance-independent evaluations free of unclosed peer results\n  when no other authorised decision is ready:\n    await decision-relevant input (event-driven attention, below)\n  record every closed result, technical triage, residual and invalidation condition\n  apply only declared conjunctions or translations\n  assign priority and boundary effect only under the current Product mandate\n  invalidate affected results when the subject or basis changes\n  update U from coverage, dependencies, conflicts and discovered materiality",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F6.%20Executive%20attention%2C%20evaluation%20and%20action%2FAttention%20cycle",
          "start_line":594
        }
      ],
      "key":"attention_cycle",
      "label":"Attention cycle"
    },
    {
      "conditions":[],
      "definition":"Five pre-activation and pre-disposition checks: outcome lock covers unchanged Goal, Product outcome, boundary, lawful re-entry class, mandate and triage policy; basis lock covers exact/current subject, authority, dependency, configuration, topology, evidence, time and candidate; Product-role lock keeps lineage identities distinct and Development Product bound to exact Install; authority lock covers unchanged semantic, evaluation, operation, decision, acceptance and publication owners/grants; coverage-and-return lock requires every material evaluation/interaction closed or explicit residual and every consumed result on its declared return relation.",
      "exceptions":[],
      "grounding":[
        {
          "end_line":675,
          "quote":"| outcome lock | the selected Goal, Product outcome, boundary and lawful re-entry class, the current MVP or release mandate, and the triage policy are unchanged |\n| basis lock | the subject, authority, dependency, configuration, topology, evidence, time and candidate coordinates are exact and current |\n| Product-role lock | the mutable Source Project, Product Definition, Release Cut, Product, Install, Artifact and dependent Product identities stay distinct, and every Development Product role stays bound to its exact underlying Install |\n| authority lock | the semantic, evaluation, operation, decision, acceptance and publication owners and grants are unchanged |\n| coverage-and-return lock | every material evaluation and interaction is closed or an explicit residual, and every consumed result followed its declared return relation |",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F6.%20Executive%20attention%2C%20evaluation%20and%20action%2FDrift%20locks",
          "start_line":671
        }
      ],
      "key":"drift_locks",
      "label":"Drift locks"
    },
    {
      "conditions":[],
      "definition":"A governed outcome's basis for one Product or an explicit directed Product chain. It records distinct mutable Source Project, current Product Definition, exact candidate checkpoint, Release Cut, Product, Install, Artifact, Development Product, dependent Product and composition-edge roles. Every Development Product binds one exact Install; each edge names source/target roles, governing authority/contracts, lifecycle, evidence boundary, refusal and invalidation.",
      "exceptions":[],
      "grounding":[
        {
          "end_line":704,
          "quote":"A governed outcome may concern one Product or an explicit directed chain of\nProducts. Its basis records the distinct role of every mutable Source\nProject, current Product Definition, exact candidate checkpoint, Release\nCut, Product, Install, Artifact, Development Product, dependent Product and\ncomposition edge. Each Development Product role binds one exact underlying\nInstall identity. Each edge names its source and target roles, its governing\nauthority and contracts, its lifecycle, its evidence boundary, its refusal\nand its invalidation (P3, P6; rc.2 #product-chain-basis; the Product-role\nmap in the basis is PRODUCT_DEFINITION §7, the lineage objects FOUNDATIONS\n§2).",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F6.%20Executive%20attention%2C%20evaluation%20and%20action%2FProduct-chain%20basis",
          "start_line":695
        }
      ],
      "key":"product_chain_basis",
      "label":"Product-chain basis"
    },
    {
      "conditions":["Bounded change and delivery management across successive tasks need separate attention."],
      "definition":"One lawful task-fit configuration allocating construction to Worker/Writer, required assessment to Reviewer and cross-task coordination/disposition within an admitted decision grant to Executive. It is not the method default or a role inventory required for all work.",
      "exceptions":["Where one sufficient frame covers the task, direct entry applies instead."],
      "grounding":[
        {
          "end_line":775,
          "quote":"It allocates construction to the Worker frame, specialised as Writer for\ndocuments and records; assessment, where it is required, to the Reviewer\nframe; and coordination across tasks to the Executive frame, which disposes\nwithin the decision grant existing authority admits (§5, §8 to §10). It is\none configuration, selected where it fits the task, not an inventory of\nroles that all work needs.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F7.%20Non-hierarchical%20frame%20configuration%2FThe%20executive%20configuration",
          "start_line":767
        }
      ],
      "key":"executive_configuration",
      "label":"Executive configuration"
    },
    {
      "conditions":[],
      "definition":"The smallest real runnable path from a supported Product entry to a material outcome through the selected composition. This profile's delivery strategy establishes it early, widens it in bounded increments, or extends/revalidates an existing affected thread. Its objective is early composition feedback at the cost of later widening.",
      "exceptions":[],
      "grounding":[
        {
          "end_line":879,
          "quote":"The Executive sequences delivery around a steel thread: the smallest real,\nrunnable path from a supported Product entry to a material outcome through\nthe selected composition. The path is established early and widened in\nbounded increments; where it already exists, the affected thread is extended\nor revalidated. Increments are chosen for consequential uncertainty,\ndependency and interface reach, and failure impact (P2; rc.2\n#steel-thread-delivery; the generic sequencing heuristic is SPEC_METHOD §8).",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F8.%20Derived%20Executive%20frame%2FSteel-thread%20delivery",
          "start_line":873
        }
      ],
      "key":"steel_thread",
      "label":"Steel thread"
    },
    {
      "conditions":[],
      "definition":"Evaluation archetype asking whether one exact current Product claim, outcome, boundary and lifecycle governs its subject without downstream reinterpretation; basis includes current Intent, Product, requirements, acceptance meaning and exact coordinates.",
      "exceptions":[],
      "grounding":[
        {
          "end_line":1019,
          "quote":"Does one exact current Product claim, outcome, boundary and lifecycle govern the claimed Product subject without downstream reinterpretation?",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F11.%20Derived%20generic%20specialist%20frame%20set",
          "start_line":1019
        }
      ],
      "key":"product_family",
      "label":"Product evaluation family"
    },
    {
      "conditions":[],
      "definition":"Evaluation archetype for one exact directed Product relation preserving source/target roles, Product Definition, Release Cut, Product and Install identities, Development Product role binding, contracts, authority, lifecycle, evidence boundary and invalidation law. Chains use bounded edge activations and declared conjunction.",
      "exceptions":[],
      "grounding":[
        {
          "end_line":1020,
          "quote":"A chain is evaluated through bounded edge activations and a declared conjunction.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F11.%20Derived%20generic%20specialist%20frame%20set",
          "start_line":1020
        }
      ],
      "key":"product_composition_family",
      "label":"Product Composition evaluation family"
    },
    {
      "conditions":[],
      "definition":"Evaluation archetype asking whether accepted structural HOW satisfies material constitutional WHAT, closes required design relations and preserves owners across affected topology.",
      "exceptions":[],
      "grounding":[
        {
          "end_line":1021,
          "quote":"Does the accepted structural HOW satisfy the material constitutional WHAT, close the required design relations and keep their owners across the affected topology?",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F11.%20Derived%20generic%20specialist%20frame%20set",
          "start_line":1021
        }
      ],
      "key":"design_family",
      "label":"Design evaluation family"
    },
    {
      "conditions":[],
      "definition":"Evaluation archetype for a bounded design component and its direct causal dependency cone, checking preservation of parent contract, internal relations, sibling seams and required outputs.",
      "exceptions":[],
      "grounding":[
        {
          "end_line":1022,
          "quote":"Does one bounded design component, with its direct causal dependency cone, preserve its parent contract, internal relations, sibling seams and required outputs?",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F11.%20Derived%20generic%20specialist%20frame%20set",
          "start_line":1022
        }
      ],
      "key":"design_component_family",
      "label":"Design Component evaluation family"
    },
    {
      "conditions":[],
      "definition":"Evaluation archetype checking that a supported public entry/exit performs exactly assigned validation, selection, transport, refusal and projection while preserving selected interior owners.",
      "exceptions":[],
      "grounding":[
        {
          "end_line":1023,
          "quote":"Does one supported public entry or exit perform exactly its assigned validation, selection, transport, refusal and projection relations while preserving the selected interior owners?",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F11.%20Derived%20generic%20specialist%20frame%20set",
          "start_line":1023
        }
      ],
      "key":"public_boundary_family",
      "label":"Public Boundary evaluation family"
    },
    {
      "conditions":[],
      "definition":"Evaluation archetype checking one semantic, artifact or runtime entity's exact identity, kind, lifecycle, owner, representation and applicable effect regime.",
      "exceptions":[],
      "grounding":[
        {
