      ],
      "key":"foundation_trace_ownership",
      "statement":"The profile imports F1 frames/context, F2 transitions/steps/configuration, F3 results/combination, F4 work state/resumption/reuse, F5 proportionality/cost, F6 claims/evidence/assessment/acceptance, F15 lineage objects and F13 work carriers. Imported consequences remain their owners' rules, not profile choices. Commitment standings are P0 recovered; P1/P2/P3/P4a/P6 independent; P4b derived from P0+P2 subject to non-reacquirable step facts; P5 derived from P0+P6 subject to the open-world premise. Selection adopts, rather than derives, I1 bounded tasks under one outcome requiring separate construction/delivery attention, I2 all decision grants held by existing authority, and I3 fallible finite-context actors with possibly probabilistic constructors. Owning clauses control conflicts; profile labels grant no meaning or authority. The trace and its consumers add no decisions beyond owners. The trace claims coverage of the lead and §§1–22, while ASSURANCE-owned terms, the trace itself and §23 dispositions add no rules. It names pillars 1–9 and neither states nor binds axiomatic-calculus rules. Profile and Product choices must not be presented as foundational consequences.",
