      "grounding":[
        {
          "end_line":321,
          "quote":"The engagement relation of this profile requires (P0, P6):\n\n- one bounded authority selects the active work and the finite frames\n  needed to evaluate it;\n- a Worker constructs one exact candidate, self-reviews, reports and stops;\n- where independent assessment is required, a separately activated\n  Reviewer acquires sufficient exact live authority, subject and evidence,\n  reusing valid computed facts while supplying its own judgment;\n- an activated Reviewer returns evidence-bound severity and technical\n  implications without becoming a second implementation loop;\n- where coordination is required, the Executive assigns priority and\n  adjudicates the current Product mandate under an existing bounded grant;\n  and\n- inability to perceive a known violation is evidence of a missing,\n  misactivated, oversized or capability-incompatible frame (RF-014).",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F4.%20Empirical%20revision%20boundary",
          "start_line":307
        }
      ],
      "key":"empirical_engagement_boundary",
      "statement":"Delivery practice and observed failure may inform frame selection, qualification and revision, but confer no method authority and import none of their originating consumer's architecture, names, actors, topology, runtime, artifacts or work stages. One bounded authority selects work and finite evaluation frames. Worker constructs one exact candidate, self-reviews, reports and stops. Required independent assessment uses a separately activated Reviewer acquiring sufficient exact live authority, subject and evidence, reusing valid computed facts but supplying its own judgment. Reviewer returns supported severity/technical implications without an implementation loop; coordination assigns priority and adjudicates the current Product mandate under an existing bounded grant. Failure to perceive a known violation evidences frame absence, misactivation, excessive size or capability mismatch. Repeated resets, long repair loops, moving review subjects, proof masking, duplicated authority and Product drift justify re-evaluation of possible declaration/activation/capability/basis/authority defects, not a definitive diagnosis, universal architecture or semantic authority. Visibility or delivery-chain participation does not turn an implementation, specialisation, scenario, dependency, installed builder or downstream Product into the authored Product.",
