      "key":"triage_support_and_decision_separation",
      "statement":"Triage fields require admissible evidence and actor capability support; missing causal/repair evidence stays explicit, with indeterminate or out_of_frame pressure where it can change evaluation, never invented precision or sideways Worker routing. The Product-owned basis binds severity/priority scales, current-boundary cutoff and its non-waivable hard stops; no universal numeric scale is imposed. Hard-stop classes are typical, not closed, and stops hold regardless of priority, cutoff or risk appetite. Severity, priority, frame result and boundary effect remain distinct even if policy maps them. None alone decides promotion blocking. A blocks projection records an EVALUATION §5 condition and returns through the core only through the one existing disposition; only disposition decides acceptance. Lower priority cannot waive a hard stop or falsified mandatory claim. An out-of-claim observation's severe label cannot open another review round. Result-dependent triage projection remains EVALUATION §4's rule.",
