      "key":"event_driven_attention_rule",
      "statement":"Default re-entry triggers are decision-relevant closed result, material exception/changed basis, owner request or declared deadline/checkpoint. During bounded Worker work with no other authorised decision ready, wait rather than repeatedly inspect unfinished work, replay unchanged judgments or request status without decision need. Retain frontier, return conditions and valid evidence/judgments; refresh materially affected support and revalidate locks before activation/disposition. Waiting waives no workspace verification, evidence validity, required independent assessment, closed-result consumption, authority or closure duty. Fallback observation declares purpose, cadence/checkpoint, evidence target and stop/escalation condition. Silence proves neither progress nor failure; unknown status alone does not establish a stall. Investigate genuine blockers/material risk and intervene where required within existing grants. Repeated no-progress or evidence-free returns require bounded reassessment and an existing-authority decision, not continued polling or identical repair on unchanged basis. Reduced churn permits neither lower assurance nor lower required capability and adds no universal cost/budget/accounting gate.",
